  "literal_analytic_proof": {
    "schema": 1,
    "kind": "ALL_WORD_STRONG_NATIVE_PERIODIC_PRINCIPAL_OPERATOR_AND_SAME_HISTORY_FILTERED_JOINT_MEASURES_NOT_PHOTON",
    "governor": {
      "plan_id": "issue-222-induced-photon-delta13-continuation-20261008",
      "captured_revision": "52ef5afc3c8cd3c8c16ff3a0fc5e358631be5219426c2b2f246a1e7b087cd9bf",
      "template_revision": "89cd9d45725622e0d65429eca9f2309508c255b54950c3a75498b6f913600efe",
      "work_item": "induced-photon",
      "requirements": [
        "outcome",
        "verification"
      ],
      "parent_sole_plan_writer": true
    },
    "premises": [
      "Use exactly the accepted full-history Hilbert, pi, Omega, translations T and L from packet45809889435fd1cfce214dd001cae2e18900ab9e0f112c3dfeca9c5aaf22ed3d/acceptance7149f6081bff118feb01d60f7d8455c3e6de59637167dda17c5ca910c1deb02a. No new independent subsequence or selected feature L. Its native family is the inherited actual minimizing physical Bloch/direct-sum ground family, translation averaged, or the accepted shrinking TOTAL spectral-support packets. No numerical ground identification is asserted.",
      "Keep fullmatrix Jordan Phi/SU4/noncompact U1, a=1/64, Lambda=2^8192, chi=2^-4096, F=2^10240, HE=HC=64, neutral heavy+active1+aux63, each canonical2V and Ref4. No bare B2, finite ground-block deletion, source/coupling/boundary replacement.",
      "The prior arc proof and actual receipt concern only selected-feature source vectors. Its face rotation, normalized Abel pointwise bound and rational radius are antecedents, not a whole-operator assertion. Full-history accepted native insertion, weighted Q propagation and every-word inequalities are the additional payment used here."
    ],
    "literal_proof": {
      "word_payment": "For every finite full history word v_N=rho_N(p)Omega_N, process the actual right-to-left insertion/propagator factorization with n0=1,E0=B0,g0=0 (or packet eta_N). A=M W_h sends n->a n, E->66a^2 E+(66d_A+16384Lambda*4096*a^2)n^2, g->a g+c_A sqrt(E); propagator dt sends E->exp(Cstar|dt|)E and preserves n,g. Include leading propagator. For sums use n_p=sum |z_j|n_j, sqrt(E_p)<=sum |z_j|sqrt(E_j), g_p=sum |z_j|g_j. B0,Cstar,d_A,c_A are EXACTLY accepted native all65 weighted costs, including shifted jets, local matter commutators, distance to weight centre and original full affine E. Thus ||v_N||<=n_p, q_Q(v_N)<=E_p uniformly N for each fixed word and compact times, NOT uniformly over word length. Norm factors are not normalized away.",
      "face_weyl_moment": "For a native face c, Dc=0,c.c=4. Put U=pi(exp(i c.A)) and R_t=pi(W_(t c/4)); inherited native Weyl relation R_t U R_t*=exp(it)U holds on FULL history by left multiplication. Weighted Cauchy gives ||p_B v_N||^2<=K_p:=E_p sum_e(c_e/4)^2/theta_e /64=E_p sum_face theta_e^-1/1024. Therefore ||(R_t-I)v_N||<=|t|sqrt(K_p). Same full-word kernels and rational-to-real flow continuity pass this bound to [p], and to words translated in time/spatially with their declared budgets. This is local electric p_B regularity, NOT regular raw unwrapped magnetic B or invariance of a static subspace.",
      "unnormalized_arcs": "Let sigma_p(I)=<[p],1_I(U)[p]>, total mass m_p=||[p]||^2<=n_p^2. Rotation of a spectral projection changes this expectation by at most 2 n_p sqrt(K_p)|t|. For M disjoint half-open arcs rotated by j*a, Ma<1 radian, sum and use invariance of projection conjugation to get sigma_p(I)<=n_p^2/M+n_p sqrt(K_p)*a*(M-1). If n_p=0 the vector is already null; no division by m_p occurs. Finite inequalities pass along the EXISTING subsequence: continuous majorants supported in slightly larger arcs and smaller inner open arcs give the same cap in the limit. Equivalently the represented Weyl relation and regularity prove this directly, avoiding endpoint Portmanteau reversals. Every point, including U=-1, has zero measure on EVERY dense word. Boundedness of the projection then implies 1_{-1}(U)=0 on the ENTIRE history Hilbert. The original spectral/null projections are used, not a seam-deleted new space.",
      "one_universal_Abel_sequence": "Use fixed rootK0=2^4100 from the antecedent and M_l=2^l, a_l=2^(-2l)/rootK0, delta_l=a_l/2, 1-r_l=delta_l/M_l; r_l is EXACT rational. All words use these SAME radii; do not tune r to a word or momentum. f_r(phi)=b_r(phi)/(2r)=sum_(k>=1) (-1)^(k+1)r^(k-1)sin(k phi)/k=Im log(1+r exp(i phi))/r. The first harmonic is identically1, and ||f_r||infty=arcsin(r)/r<=pi/2: the circle of radius r centered at1 subtends maximal angle arcsin(r), and convex arcsin lies below its endpoint chord on[0,1]. Let F=principal(U)/2, standard principal in[-pi,pi); at the seam radial f_r=0 but F=-pi/2. The zero seam projection already paid on ALL words removes this discrepancy without changing the Hilbert or null quotient.",
      "all_word_error": "Off the seam arc of length2delta, |f_r-F|<=8(1-r)/delta for r>=1/2; on it |f_r-F|<=pi<4. Thus ||(f_r_l(U)-F)[p]||^2 <=64 n_p^2/M_l^2+16[n_p^2/M_l+(n_p sqrt(K_p)/rootK0)(M_l-1)/M_l^2], which tends to zero for EVERY fixed p. The same estimate is N-uniform on arbitrary finite history words, not just Omega or phase-polynomial vectors. Continuous f_r(U) already acts on the full accepted representation: its absolutely convergent series is a norm limit of finite phase polynomials. No new extraction is used for it or for F.",
      "strong_operator_upgrade": "Since ||f_r_l(U)||,||F||<=pi/2, convergence on the dense full-word set extends to ALL H_hist: for arbitrary v choose [p] close, bound error by pi||v-[p]|| plus the paid word error. Therefore F is a genuine bounded selfadjoint native periodic principal operator on the ENTIRE H_hist. In particular the strong limit descends through the original null ideal since ||f_r p||<=pi/2||p||. Strong limits of uniformly bounded products obey A_l B_l v-A B v=A_l(B_l-B)v+(A_l-A)Bv; this preserves any finite mixed product with native bounded history letters, adjoints, translated faces and limiting principal operators, in their ACTUAL order. It does NOT say F commutes with electric boosts. R_t F(U)R_t*=F(exp(it)U) is Borel covariance, not F(U)+t/2. Products and original seam/null projections are preserved; no compressed selected-feature multiplication is substituted.",
      "same_L_filter_graph": "Only now set P0=1_{0}(L), Q=I-P0 for the SAME accepted full-history L. For fixed epsilon>0 and any bounded principal/history product B, define X_(epsilon,B)=epsilon(L+epsilon)^-1 Q B Omega. It belongs to D(L) because E*epsilon/(E+epsilon)<=epsilon. ||X||<=||B Omega||, ||LX||<=epsilon||B Omega||. If B_l->B strongly with bounded products, the filtered insertions converge in graph norm, with squared graph error<= (1+epsilon^2)||(B_l-B)Omega||^2. This is not an unfiltered principal domain theorem, small-form-to-small-graph inference, static dynamics or identification Q_N=Q. Entire limiting kerL, including collapsed finite excitations, is removed AFTER L exists.",
      "native_joint_and_cross_kernels": "Let a,b label orientations or arbitrary fixed bounded principal/history products, v_a=B_a Omega, and E_joint be the already constructed commuting T,L spectral resolution. Define mu_ab(dq,dE)=<v_a,Q E_joint(dq,dE)Q v_b>, supported E>0. It is a finite positive MATRIX measure, with total diagonal<=||v_a||^2 and mixed variation<=||v_a||||v_b||. Set s_e(E)=epsilon/(E+epsilon). The insertion/graph kernels are <X_a,T(x)exp(itL)X_b>=integral exp(iq.x+itE)s_e^2 dmu_ab, <LX_a,T(x)exp(itL)X_b>=integral exp(iq.x+itE)E s_e^2 dmu_ab and <LX_a,T(x)exp(itL)LX_b>=integral exp(iq.x+itE)E^2 s_e^2 dmu_ab. Their total variations are respectively bounded by ||v_a||||v_b||,epsilon||v_a||||v_b||,epsilon^2||v_a||||v_b||. For any other same-L vector y (including a proved electric/current vector if supplied), cross kernels use mu_ay=<v_a,Q E_joint Q y> and ONE s_e factor when only a is filtered, with graph factor E s_e. Cauchy pays mixed tails; no independent electric or principal feature generator may be substituted.",
      "weak_passage_not_pointwise": "Strong source convergence bounds Fourier kernels uniformly in x,t by Hilbert Cauchy, and hence weak joint measures against continuous BZ and bounded-energy tests in THIS representation. The fixed-epsilon E s_e multiplier pays graph passage. At finite N Parseval only gives BZ-average error; in the infinite representation total joint variation tends to zero. Neither statement implies an a.e density exists, a value at q, pointwise small-q convergence or infrared scaling. Finite Q_N spectral measures are NOT used to infer these measures. Spatial covariance follows T(x)F_0 T(-x)=F_x from bounded strong limits."
    },
    "residual_IR_gate": {
      "definition": "For shrinking BZ annuli A_k approaching nonzero q=0, C_k=mu(A_k x (0,infinity))/m_BZ(A_k) is the wholeP0-removed matrix covariance average. For a prescribed positive cone speed c and relative band delta_k->0, W_k=mu({q in A_k, |E-c|q||<=delta_k|q|})/m_BZ(A_k). A sharp commoncone additionally requires a rank-two transverse matrix ATOM in the disintegration at E=c|q|, nonzero correctly scaled fixed-source residue, and vanishing off-cone weight. Absolute continuity/disintegration and covariance scaling themselves require proof. Annulus averages are necessary gates, not sufficient pointwise assertions.",
      "computed_from_paid_inputs": "For each local normalized principal face, M^2=pi^2/4 bounds total unfiltered and filtered diagonal masses. Thus for EACH annulus paid inputs give 0<=C_k<=M^2/m_BZ(A_k), 0<=W_k<=M^2/m_BZ(A_k), and 0<=atomic_mass<=W_k. For filtered mass replace integrand by s_e^2; in any candidate positive band s_e^2 has a known positive lower and upper factor, but no unfiltered lower exists. The certified uniform low-q covariance lower, cone-weight lower and atom/residue lower are ALL EXACTLY ZERO. Their upper envelopes diverge as annulus measure shrinks. No local phase nonatomicity supplies energy nonatomicity or energy atoms. CLI evaluates exact conservative rational upper envelopes with pi/2<2 and different annulus volumes; it does not invent actual covariance values.",
      "source_weakening_rejected": "First harmonic1 is fixed. Multiplying by a q-dependent vanishing factor changes the observable and multiplies covariance/residue by its square; it cannot satisfy the original gate. Resolvent filtering only multiplies an existing measure by positive smooth s_e^2 on E>0; it cannot create an atom from a diffuse measure, and cannot establish that an atom exists. Neither low energy, filtering, positivity, a contact sumrule nor phase seam nonatomicity proves a photon.",
      "status": "UNPAID_FROM_AVAILABLE_INPUTS_NOT_CAMPAIGN_COMPLETION"
    },
    "scope": {
      "entire_history_strong_principal_operator_conditional": true,
      "same_L_fixed_epsilon_D_L_graph": true,
      "weak_joint_BZ_energy_and_cross_kernels": true,
